🟠 Topic 3: Variables & Expressions
🔹 Why Variables?

👉 Avoid hardcoding values
👉 Make code reusable across:

dev / stage / prod
🔹 1. Input Variables
Define (variables.tf)
variable "instance_type" {
  default = "t2.micro"
}
Use (main.tf)
resource "aws_instance" "demo" {
  instance_type = var.instance_type
}
🔹 Ways to Pass Variables
1. CLI
terraform apply -var="instance_type=t3.micro"
2. .tfvars file
instance_type = "t3.micro"
terraform apply -var-file="dev.tfvars"
🔹 2. Output Values

👉 Used to display useful info

output "public_ip" {
  value = aws_instance.demo.public_ip
}

✔ After apply → shows EC2 IP

🔹 3. Local Values

👉 For internal reuse (clean code)

locals {
  env = "dev"
}

Use:

tags = {
  Environment = local.env
}
🔹 4. Data Sources (🔥 Important)

👉 Fetch existing resources (NOT create)

data "aws_ami" "latest" {
  most_recent = true
  owners      = ["amazon"]
}

Use:

ami = data.aws_ami.latest.id
🔹 5. Expressions & Functions
Example Functions:
upper("dev")      → "DEV"
length(["a","b"]) → 2
Conditional Expression:
instance_type = var.env == "prod" ? "t3.large" : "t2.micro"
🔥 Real DevOps Example
variable "env" {}

resource "aws_instance" "demo" {
  instance_type = var.env == "prod" ? "t3.large" : "t2.micro"

  tags = {
    Environment = var.env
  }
}

👉 Same code → different environments

